  "visualBrief": "Specific Somanathapura Chennakesava standing temple: three stellate stone shrine towers/walls, stepped shared jagati platform, low east-facing mandapa and recessed doorway, original simplified figure/niche/miniature-shrine/frieze vocabulary, patterned receding tower registers and domical caps/finials. Picture-led approximate low enclosing open pillared corridor, east entrance pavilion/short stairs and separate plain stone pillar. Existing shared stone/material graphs; no copied narrative/deity/text atlas, full ritual interior or broad courtyard ground slab.",
