  "sourceFacts": {
    "horizontalBasis": "Named standard PMTiles Keshava Temple archaeological-site point35184523899922 correlates the main lobed building35184523899920. No exact-QID building attribution claimed. Anchor76.88155573,12.27573677; heading0, internal local+x angle-.13rad, entrance approximately east/local+x. Three lobe centers establish west/north/south shrine stations; the eastern lobe establishes the mandapa. Standard map does not resolve the enclosing corridor: its68x52m approximate picture-led footprint is fitted to open surroundings and the east footway, with no mapped dimension claim. Native toilet point and remote independent building stay outside it.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Ordinary-picture/map visualization estimates, not survey dimensions: main mapped envelope about31x25m, three shrine centers in west/north/south lobes, approximately8.4m shrine width,1.15m jagati, temple eaves6.2m, four receding tower registers to10.3m, domical caps/finials to11.5m above the local base. Mandapa roof about6.2m and low central crest7.1m. Enclosure about68x52m with4.4m-deep open corridors,3.4m columns/eaves, separate4.5m-high gate pavilion and approximately8m plain pillar. Hidden layout, sculptural counts, damage and exact thresholds remain approximate."
  },
